<p>Germany’s Greens narrowly edged Chancellor Friedrich Merz’s conservative CDU in the Baden-Württemberg state election. Early projections and exit polls put the Greens around 30–31%, with the CDU just under 30%. The result matters beyond the state: Baden-Württemberg is a major industrial hub, and the vote is an early test of public mood in a year packed with elections across Germany. Cem Özdemir, a prominent Green politician, is in line to succeed outgoing premier Winfried Kretschmann and could become the first leader of a German federal state with Turkish roots—a notable step for political representation. Projections also show the far-right Alternative for Germany (AfD) nearly doubling its 2021 result to about 18%, a sign of an increasingly fragmented political landscape.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/MLIvp9lSJdTUdTqRBwgnpcjnbcrABVf7A2wankpNo6k-cUjWEQyDSEB9QfRi8iGIDPwAtA0WmMZ0xfLe1pK0tc65lbHdGrJ63VZD-5F-' alt='Greens’ candidate Cem Özdemir addresses supporters after exit polls in Baden-Württemberg.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>SPD setback: Politico said the Social Democratic Party (SPD), Merz’s coalition partner, was on track for its worst result ever in a federal or state election.</li><li>Auto anxieties: Politico reported that the AfD posted the biggest gains in vote share by tapping anxieties around Baden-Württemberg’s struggling auto industry.</li><li>Next contests: Rhineland-Palatinate votes later in March, and eastern states vote in September, where outlets expect stronger AfD performances.</li></ul><blockquote>What a tremendous comeback! - Cem Özdemir</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>Cem Özdemir (Greens): Özdemir told supporters the result marked a comeback for the Greens as polls closed. (<a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/germany-greens-win-state-vote-friedrich-merz-coalition/'>Politico Europe</a>)</li><li>German broadcasters (ARD/ZDF): Exit polls showed a razor-thin Greens–CDU race, with the final outcome still sensitive to late-counted results. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980006/german-state-election-deals-blow-to-merz-exit-polls'>Dawn</a>)</li><li>Campaign dynamics (Dawn/AFP): Dawn said the CDU held sizable polling leads earlier in the campaign, but the race tightened sharply in the final stretch before election day. (<a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980006/german-state-election-deals-blow-to-merz-exit-polls'>Dawn</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.dawn.com/news/1980006/german-state-election-deals-blow-to-merz-exit-polls'>German state election deals blow to Merz: exit polls</a> - dawn.com</li><li><a href='https://www.economist.com/europe/2026/03/08/germanys-greens-have-come-back-to-win-in-baden-wurttemberg'>Germany’s Greens have come back to win in Baden-Württemberg</a> - economist.com</li><li><a href='https://japantoday.com/category/world/german-greens-lead-chancellor-merz%27s-conservatives-in-state-election2'>German Greens lead Chancellor Merz&#x27;s conservatives in state election</a> - japantoday.com</li><li><a href='https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-greens-narrowly-win-baden-württemberg-election/live-76265491'>Germany news: Greens narrowly win Baden-Württemberg election</a> - dw.com</li><li><a href='https://www.politico.eu/article/germany-greens-win-state-vote-friedrich-merz-coalition/'>Germany’s Greens set to win key state vote in blow to Merz’s coalition</a> - politico.eu</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/5e3630ee-8353-44b5-97f5-de6bba7e2a20'>German chancellor’s party heads for narrow defeat in key regional election</a> - ft.com</li></ul>